WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.785 --> 00:00:07.686
After lunch on Saturday, Jackie rolled her bike from Grandma's garage. She called Poke, and he

2
00:00:07.687 --> 00:00:14.462
ran alongside her as she biked to Hudson's house. Hudson's family lived less than a mile away

3
00:00:14.463 --> 00:00:20.445
in a log cabin tucked among some cedar trees. He'd asked Jackie to bring Poke over

4
00:00:20.446 --> 00:00:23.779
this afternoon. Poke was going to help with some dog training. Jackie found her friend in

5
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:31.591
the obstacle course behind the house. Hudson had built the course himself from old boards and other

6
00:00:31.592 --> 00:00:37.678
items he had found around the property. It was a crazy collection of bars, planks, tables,

7
00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:42.595
and tunnels. Hudson waved to Jackie and then turned back to his dog, Bart. He was running

8
00:00:42.596 --> 00:00:53.351
the beagle through the course. "Sit," Jackie whispered to Poke, and together they watched the training

9
00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:59.500
session. Hudson motioned at Bart to keep him moving through the course. When Bart tried to

10
00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:08.652
skip a tunnel, Hudson immediately stopped him. He showed the tunnel to the dog, and this time

11
00:01:08.653 --> 00:01:13.969
Bart followed the course properly. "Good boy!" Hudson said as the dog leaped onto an end

12
00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:24.313
table and gobbled the treat Hudson held out. "Yip! Yip!" Bart barked. "Whuff." Poke looked at

13
00:01:24.314 --> 00:01:27.313
Jackie. She pulled a treat from her pocket. "Good boy. You sat quietly." "Thanks for bringing Poke

14
00:01:27.314 --> 00:01:36.381
over," Hudson said. "Bart loves his buddy, Poke, but he needs to learn to ignore him

15
00:01:36.382 --> 00:01:45.201
when he is working." "No problem," said Jackie. "It looks like you're doing a great job with

16
00:01:45.202 --> 00:01:56.029
Bart." She scratched the beagle's ears. "He seems really smart." "He is. He still goes around

17
00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:06.104
some of the jumps," said Hudson, "but he's learning. He's just a little over a year

18
00:02:06.105 --> 00:02:15.431
old and already knows all the commands." Hudson had shown his family's beagles in junior handlers events

19
00:02:15.432 --> 00:02:23.186
for years, but Bart was the first dog he had trained for agility competition. In agility,

20
00:02:23.187 --> 00:02:26.995
Hudson was going to compete against handlers of all ages. Jackie knew it would be challenging.

21
00:02:26.996 --> 00:02:35.508
Hudson and Jackie let the two dogs play together for a few minutes. Bart ran circles around

22
00:02:35.509 --> 00:02:40.339
the bigger dog, bowing low and barking happily. Hudson grinned. "They have different personalities, don't they?"

23
00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.414
Jackie nodded. "I guess that's because Bart is younger than Poke. Plus, they were bred for

24
00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:56.409
different jobs. Labradors are supposed to retrieve ducks, and beagles are supposed to chase rabbits. Different jobs

25
00:02:56.410 --> 00:03:05.642
for different dogs." The dogs stopped playing and lay there, panting. Then they took off together

26
00:03:05.643 --> 00:03:13.551
again. "Speaking of different breeds," said Jackie, "I've got a little problem." She explained about Poke's retirement.

27
00:03:13.552 --> 00:03:17.710
"Grandma wants me to show Esmerelda, but I don't know . . ." Hudson raised his

28
00:03:17.711 --> 00:03:23.209
eyebrows. "All that blow-drying and brushing?" Jackie laughed. "Exactly! I don't even like to comb my

29
00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:33.040
own hair!" "Obviously," Hudson joked. Jackie grinned. She was used to her friends teasing her about her

30
00:03:33.041 --> 00:03:41.784
messy hair. Then she elbowed Hudson in the side. "But seriously, I have a problem. The

31
00:03:41.785 --> 00:03:48.863
next junior handlers show is only a month away." Jackie's throat tightened as she thought about

32
00:03:48.864 --> 00:03:53.854
her second-place ribbon from last week. Her friends had been kind and encouraging—after they had finished making

33
00:03:53.855 --> 00:04:01.496
jokes about Poke giving the judge a bath. But Jackie still felt like a failure. It

34
00:04:01.497 --> 00:04:09.932
was as if everybody could ride a real bike while she still had training wheels. She swallowed

35
00:04:09.933 --> 00:04:18.410
hard. "I need a first-place win to make it to open class. But I don't have

36
00:04:18.411 --> 00:04:32.575
a dog." Bart came running over, his body wiggling madly. Poke ambled behind the smaller dog

37
00:04:32.576 --> 00:04:37.493
and then plopped down beside Jackie. "Didn't your grandma buy one of Bart's littermates?" Hudson asked. "Yes.

38
00:04:37.494 --> 00:04:42.992
Grandma hasn't shown Howler yet, but she's been working with him a lot." "Bart's doing his

39
00:04:42.993 --> 00:04:50.238
first junior handlers show next month. We'd both have beagles at the event. That would be

40
00:04:50.239 --> 00:05:01.875
fun." Jackie stared at the little beagle chasing a leaf as it blew across the grass. "I

41
00:05:01.876 --> 00:05:11.522
don't know. I've never shown a small dog." Hudson shrugged. "It's no big deal. You'll be

42
00:05:11.523 --> 00:05:17.703
competing in the novice class, so you won't compete against me. I compete in the open class."

43
00:05:17.704 --> 00:05:21.774
Jackie raised her eyebrows. "Do you think I'm scared of competing against you?" "Nope!" Hudson said

44
00:05:21.775 --> 00:05:33.124
quickly. "I didn't say that." Jackie watched him out of the corner of her eye. He

45
00:05:33.125 --> 00:05:39.266
hadn't said it, but did he think it? After all, she was still stuck in novice class.

46
00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:47.584
"I think it would be fun," Hudson repeated. "We could train the beagles together sometimes." Jackie

47
00:05:47.585 --> 00:05:51.580
was still unsure. "I've always worked with Labradors. I'd be working with a totally different type

48
00:05:51.581 --> 00:05:57.579
of dog." "You don't have a Labrador to show right now," Hudson said. "So you're definitely going

49
00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:05.085
to have to learn about a new breed. Why not beagles?" Bart pounced on Poke's tail.

50
00:06:05.086 --> 00:06:10.742
The big dog lifted his head and then rolled over. "The whole idea of junior handlers

51
00:06:10.743 --> 00:06:17.058
is to learn about showing dogs," Hudson went on. "You're not expected to be an expert. That's

52
00:06:17.059 --> 00:06:27.221
what novice class is for—being a beginner." "But beagles—" "Are fun," Hudson said firmly. "Plus, I'll

53
00:06:27.222 --> 00:06:32.568
help you. The secret to beagles is learning their personality." "Hmm . . ." Jackie looked at

54
00:06:32.569 --> 00:06:35.647
her dog. "What do you think, Poke?" He rested his head on her leg. "I agree,"

55
00:06:35.648 --> 00:06:41.449
she said with a laugh. "Nothing is better than a Labrador. I wish Shadow was older—she's

56
00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:46.050
one of Grandma's new Lab puppies." "Well, keep thinking about beagles," Hudson said. He got up and

57
00:06:46.051 --> 00:06:56.554
took Bart back to the obstacle course. The little dog stood at the starting line, his

58
00:06:56.555 --> 00:07:01.615
gaze fixed on Hudson. He was obviously eager to please his master. "I've got a whole

59
00:07:01.616 --> 00:07:05.865
month to practice," Jackie thought. "And I really want to enter the November show." Maybe Howler wasn't

60
00:07:05.866 --> 00:07:16.011
a bad choice. Back at the obstacle course, Bart ran fast, panting all the way. At

61
00:07:16.012 --> 00:07:27.937
the end he stuck his nose in the air and howled. Hudson rubbed his head and gave

62
00:07:27.938 --> 00:07:42.103
him a treat. The little dog immediately bounded back to the starting line and looked at

63
00:07:42.104 --> 00:07:47.156
Hudson. He was ready to run the course again. "Whoa," Jackie thought. "He's got so much

64
00:07:47.157 --> 00:07:54.648
energy!" She sighed. Working with a beagle seemed very different from working with a Labrador retriever. If

65
00:07:54.649 --> 00:08:03.641
she did choose to work with Howler, Hudson had better keep his promise about helping her.

